@startuml possession-flow-turnover
' ⚠ A DETAIL DIAGRAM. The whole possession, and the second-chance LOOP that
' wraps this one, are in possession-flow.puml — read that first.
' ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS: the turnover gate, the nine causes, and the charge's
' second event. Every path here ENDS the possession.
' ⚠ Notes say what the flow DOES; the argument lives in possession-flow-model.md.
' Render: plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng   (every diagram is now under
'   the 4096px default, so the flag is insurance — but keep using it, and ⚠ keep each
'   diagram SCREEN-SIZED: past ~2,000px it stops being readable long before it stops
'   rendering. ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out and does not catch deprecated syntax
'   that renders as a warning box — look at the PNG.)
title TurnoverResolver — the nine causes\n//§3.9 causes · §3.16 the charge//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start
if (**turnover?**\n//ballSecurity vs stealing/individualDefense//\n//× defensiveScheme pressure//\n//× fatigueFactor per player//) then (yes)
  note right
    The gate decides IF; a weighted nine-way draw then picks WHICH
    cause — re-partitioning the label without moving the count.
    Leans: SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION on //acumen//↓ × //defensiveScheme//↑;
    OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS on //teamOffense//↓. STOLEN stays
    dominant. Every cause charges the ball-handler.
  end note
  if (cause == STOLEN?\n//weighted nine-way draw//) then (yes)
    :TURNOVER — STOLEN
    primaryPlayerId = the ball-handler (the victim)
    **opponentPlayerId = the STEALER**
    stealer.recordSteal() — the box-score credit;
    note right
      The stealer lands ON THE EVENT — ONE row, not two: there is no
      PlayType.STEAL. ⚠ **The rule that decides that**, and governs
      any future participant: **second PARTICIPANT → a column; second ACCOUNTING → an event; neither → nothing.** A steal has
      a participant, so it takes the column; the charge below has an
      accounting consequence a column cannot carry (isInBonus counts
      FOUL EVENTS), so it keeps its two events.
      ⚠ **NO NEW DRAW** — pickStealer runs at the same point in the
      stream; only the declaration was hoisted so the value reaches
      addEvent.
    end note
  else (no)
    :TURNOVER — one of
    SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION / OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS /
    TRAVELLING / LOST_BALL_OUT_OF_BOUNDS / 3_SECONDS_VIOLATION /
    8_SECONDS_BACKCOURT_VIOLATION / OVER_AND_BACK
    //no stealer credited//;
    note right
      ⚠ **opponentPlayerId is NULL on all eight — a DECISION, not an omission.** Seven have no counterparty at all. A charge
      does have one (the defender who drew it) but the engine
      never picks one; doing so needs a new draw and would shift
      the stream.
    end note
    if (**cause == OFFENSIVE_FOUL?**\n//the charge / illegal screen — a PERSONAL FOUL by rule//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — OFFENSIVE_FOUL
      charge the BALL-HANDLER //recordFoul()//
      committingTeamId = **OFFENSE** — so the DEFENSE gains the bonus;
      note right
        ⚠ **TWO EVENTS FOR ONE OCCURRENCE** — the TURNOVER above and
        this FOUL both describe the same charge. Any reconciliation
        that counts events must tolerate it.
         **One of only two sites where the committer is on OFFENSE**
        (the other is the rebounding foul), so it is the only other
        path that puts the DEFENSIVE team in the bonus.
         **NOT flagrant-eligible** — the flagrant roll lives in
        FoulResolver and this path never reaches it. It is a personal
        foul: counts toward the bonus and FOUL_OUT_LIMIT.
      end note
    endif
  endif
  :**possession over**;
  stop
else (no)
  :→ on to FoulResolver
  //possession-flow.puml//;
  stop
endif
@enduml
